Scope and changes
-----------------
This revision uses kvzalloc for submit_create's combined structure, BO and
command tables, and kvfree at both early errors and final destruction.
It replaces the original draft's independent SZ_128K count caps with:
  if (sz > KMALLOC_MAX_SIZE) return ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);
The existing size_add/struct_size/array_size arithmetic saturates overflow.
The check preserves the previous configurable allocation ceiling and
oversize errno; it is not a quota for all submission-related memory.

Source/lifetime review
----------------------
Reviewed original draft and 7.3-rc5 base. The relevant code is unchanged.
All msm_gem_submit_put call sites are the ioctl completion, retirement,
and msm_job_free. Retirement executes from retire_worker/recover_worker;
scheduler release executes from drm_sched_free_job_work or
 dr m_sched_entity_kill_jobs_work (identifier: drm_sched_entity_kill_jobs_work).
Relevant spinlocks are released before final puts. Allocation is from the
ioctl with GFP_KERNEL. A3xx a3xx_submit reads CPU bookkeeping and writes
separate command-buffer IOVAs/sizes into the ring; the GPU does not consume
the submit structure's own address. No new DMA/SG mapping is needed.

KMALLOC_MAX_SIZE = 1UL << (MAX_PAGE_ORDER + PAGE_SHIFT). In the recorded
Fedora config PAGE_SHIFT=12 and CONFIG_ARCH_FORCE_MAX_ORDER=10, giving
4 MiB. Default arm64 16K/64K configs allow 32 MiB/512 MiB respectively.
The aggregate guard therefore avoids imposing new per-count policy.
128K of both recorded entry types would permit 9,437,536 bytes;
64K of both would permit 4,718,944 bytes while rejecting some formerly
admissible BO-heavy submissions below the old byte ceiling.

